# Plan documents

When the user asks for a plan document (or a file whose purpose is an implementation/rollout plan):

- Location and name: Write it under `docs/` with filename prefix `PLAN-` (e.g. `docs/PLAN-feature-name.md`).
- Tone and shape: Keep it very terse. Short lines, plain language, scannable in a few seconds.
- Markdown — use sparingly: Prefer a single top-level title (`# Plan: …`) then plain paragraphs and simple `-` bullets. Avoid tables, blockquotes, emoji, and deep heading hierarchies (`##` / `###` only when they genuinely separate major chunks). Avoid bold/italic except where one emphasis per section helps scanning. Skip horizontal rules unless they separate two large phases. Use fenced code blocks only for real code, paths, or API snippets — not for prose.
- Goal: Someone glancing at the raw file or a preview should grasp phases, dependencies, and done criteria without parsing heavy formatting.
